  "summary": {
    "intent": "Resolve review findings and merge conflicts on stacked PRs #480 (change 278) and #483 (change 281) in the caliper repo so they can be approved and merged, then address two newly open findings on those same changes.",
    "outcome": "Fixed the discriminant_prop finding on #480 (df5a1503) and resolved it, merged main into both branches clearing conflicts, and pushed #483 (ac03d894) after 1629 workspace tests passed. Two new findings remain open; workers were dispatched to fix factory callback param defaults (278) and stale `used` in the lazy delta (281), with push and resolve pending their reports.",
    "learnings": {
      "repo": [
        "Rust toolchain is pinned via PATH to ~/.rustup/toolchains/1.99.1-aarch64-apple-darwin and builds use a separate CARGO_TARGET_DIR (caliper-fixtures/shrink/target-mf) to avoid clobbering other target dirs.",
        "Full verification uses `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked --no-fail-fast`; quick checks use `cargo check --workspace --all-targets` plus `cargo test -p caliper-docgen-core --lib`.",
        "Branches for changes are pushed to differently named remote branches (local fix-480-disc -> origin feat/factory-own-props; local mf5-483 -> origin feat/relevance-output).",
        "`add_absent` must keep other.discriminant_prop when self has none, mirroring `merge_parent`; otherwise factory render callbacks with `Props = A | B` lose discriminantProp and TOON omits the discriminator.",
        "The factory path never calls `extract_param_defaults`, so callback destructuring defaults (e.g. `size = 'M'`) are not captured; normal components use that function.",
        "Lazy sessions can leave a retained answer's `used` list stale after a consumer-JSX-only edit because it doesn't appear in `updated_keys`; the fix should reuse the eager path's relevance rule so there is one owner."
      ],
      "code": [],
      "workflow": [
        "Entire trail findings are listed with `entire trail finding list caliper/<change> --freshness=any` and resolved with `entire trail finding resolve <id> --branch ... -m <message>`, with the resolution message citing commit sha and test evidence.",
        "Validate a regression test by confirming it fails without the fix and passes with it (done by reverting the fix).",
        "Merge main into stacked PR branches to clear DIRTY merge state; PR status then shows BLOCKED pending approval.",
        "Delegating findings to parallel worker agents (Sonnet for 278, Opus for 281) that don't push, with the orchestrator pushing and resolving after they report, keeps push/resolve under one owner."
      ]
